; The DEPENDENCY of the component face's cross-crate fixture family. Generated with
; `--component=true`, so it publishes BOTH cross-crate artifacts a consumer needs: its
; `extern-interface/dep/**` export (which puts these names in the consumer's spec namespace) and its
; `component/wit/**` package (which says how they cross the component boundary).
;
; Deliberately a real generated dependency rather than the stub tree `tests/extern-deps-wasm` uses:
; a stub has no component face at all, which is exactly the case import mode is OPT-IN for.

; A record. Projects to a `resource` with a constructor and getters, so a consumer importing it gets
; a type it can both mint and read — the shape the whole seam exists to share.
token = [ name: text, amount: uint ]

; A second record, so a consumer can hold two dependency types at once and the `use` line has to
; carry both names rather than one.
policy = [ id: bytes ]

; A transparent alias. The consumer resolves it THROUGH to `uint`, so it must NOT appear in the
; consumer's `use` line — the negative control for the import resolution.
coin = uint

; Nothing here is unprojectable, deliberately: this dependency is COMPILED as part of the cross-crate
; build check, so every rule has to be a rust type a crate can hold. The dependency whose WIT
; excludes a type — the exclusion-propagation case — is `../dep-unexported`, which is projected but
; never built.
